#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automake Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:337 kdevelop-survey.docbook:360
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:378 kdevelop-survey.docbook:384
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>projects</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>automake</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>automake</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:341 kdevelop-survey.docbook:364
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:382 kdevelop-survey.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>projects</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Projects created with &kdevelop;'s &automanag; make it very easy for "
"developers to use the &GNU; standard development tools. They provide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "a better way of <filename>Makefile</filename> generation and"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"a good and safe way for fast adaption towards different systems by autoconf-"
"generated <filename>configure</filename> scripts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "QMake Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>qmake</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>qmake</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For developers who enjoy the flexibility and feel of &Qt;'s qmake system, "
"&kdevelop; offers the ability to handle qmake based projects (.pro files) "
"within the &GUI;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on the QMake project manager see the <quote>qmake User "
"Guide</quote> which should be included in your distribution or have a look "
"at the <ulink url=\"http://doc.trolltech.com/\">TROLLTECH Documentation</"
"ulink> home page where you may find the QMake documentation of your "
"<quote>Qt C++ GUI Application Development Toolkit</quote> version."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "ANT Projects (&Java; Projects)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>ant</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>ant</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:385 kdevelop-survey.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>Java</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Java</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "development"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&Java; developers may want to use the Apache ANT project manager for their "
"projects. To set up a new Ant project in &kdevelop; select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New Project...</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Java</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Ant Project</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Application</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information see <ulink url=\"http://ant.apache.org/\">The Apache "
"Ant Project</ulink> home page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "custom"
msgstr "personalisat"

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>custom projects</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid "Makefile"
msgstr "Makefile"

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>custom projects</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you prefer to maintain your own <filename>Makefiles</filename> for your "
"project you may use the custom project option of &kdevelop;. This may be "
"feasible in unusually structured projects or if you want to retain full "
"control over the <command>make</command> process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yet, if you do not <emphasis>really need</emphasis> the extra flexibility "
"and control of the custom project manager you should consider &automanag; or "
"one of the other project managers, because they considerably ease the "
"program building and distribution processes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Distribute Your Application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>distribution</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "application"
msgstr "aplicacion"

#. Tag: secondary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>distribution</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "binary packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The distribution of your applications does not require the end-user to have "
"anything different installed other than"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "an appropriate compiler,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid "a linker, and"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "the appropriate development libraries,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"which at least for C++ applications is most often the case. But you can as "
"well distribute <emphasis>binary packages</emphasis> of your application. In "
"either way, the end-user of your product does not need &kdevelop; installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For giving away your sources, we advise to include the <emphasis>project "
"file</emphasis> of &kdevelop; as well. This makes it very easy for other "
"developers&mdash;if they use &kdevelop;&mdash;to work with your sources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For projects where <emphasis>several developers</emphasis>, maybe working on "
"different places, are involved, this should be the case anyway. So you can "
"ensure consistency of the <filename>Makefiles</filename> to not run into "
"trouble."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdevelop-survey.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Especially on multi language applications, <emphasis>translators</emphasis> "
"won't actually work with the source code, except in cases that require "
"correction for enabling translation support."
msgstr ""

